cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Exact computational certificates for "Ledger defects, harmonic obstructions
  for 2-Stein models, and horospherical rigidity"
message: >-
  If you use these certificates, please cite both the software and the
  accompanying paper.
type: software
abstract: >-
  Four self-contained Python scripts verifying, by exact arithmetic, the
  algebraic identities of the six-dimensional 2-Stein family A^theta studied
  in the accompanying paper. Coefficients are represented in the quotient ring
  Z[s,c]/(s^2+c^2-1) or in Q, and every asserted identity is reduced exactly;
  no floating-point arithmetic and no external computer algebra system is
  used. The scripts check the curvature symmetries and both Bianchi
  identities, the differentiated 2-Stein equations, the norm identities
  |B|^2 = 4608 s^2 and tr(B_X^2) = 288 s^2 a b^2, the third Ledger constant
  -2176, the cubic contractions of A^theta, and the harmonic-realizability
  obstruction F_A = 2176 - 162 s^2 together with its directional violation
  -162 s^2 at X = e_1.
